// TEST: An array literal over a leading opaque RaggedIdx is refused (rejects)
// ============================================================================
// Gap G190 (a), lead decision 2026-11-09: `RaggedIdx<_>` (the opaque form a
// row PEELED from a ragged parent carries) as the ONLY slot of an array
// LITERAL has no outer axis to vary its row lengths over. The interpreter
// read `[2.0]` as a plain rank-1 array while the C++ lane refused it in
// codegen (BL7004, "ragged literal value count (1) does not match sum of row
// lengths (0)"). It is refused at lowering in every lane, with the first-slot
// RaggedIdx diagnostic (index-types/020's BL4003).
// ============================================================================
type A = Array<Float64 like RaggedIdx<_>>
let mut backing: A = [2.0]
let s = reduce(backing, (+))
// ERROR: BL4003
// ERROR-CONTAINS: RaggedIdx requires at least one prior index
// REJECT-AT: lower
